From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] cuda/hip: RDNA4 wave32 DPP reductions + float4 access in gated_delta_net

The gated_delta_net recurrence kernel (13.1% of pp512, ~4.8% of decode,
9.2% of the 16k phase after the 0023-state profile) runs one warp per
state column with a serial token loop. On gfx1201 the ISA shows the two
warp_reduce_sum calls per token lower __shfl_xor to ds_bpermute_b32 -
ten LDS round-trips per token, each followed by a full s_wait_dscnt 0x0 -
and the k/q/state accesses issue as strided scalar global_load_b32.

Two changes, HIP-guarded to gfx120x so the CUDA path is untouched:

1. DPP butterfly reduction: quad_perm xor1/xor2, row_half_mirror,
   row_mirror, then v_permlanex16 across the two 16-lane rows. Five
   VALU-issued adds per reduction, zero LDS traffic, no data-counter
   waits. Falls back to the generic warp_reduce_sum on any other
   arch/wave size.

2. float4 vectorization: lane row-ownership remapped from
   i = r*warp_size + lane to i = lane*4 + r for the S_v==128 wave32
   case, so state/k/q loads and state stores become single dwordx4
   accesses (11 loads/token -> 5). Host launch gates this on 16-byte
   alignment of all row bases and strides (falls back to the scalar
   mapping template otherwise); both mappings are plain permutations of
   the same reduction terms.

Kernel-level (test-backend-ops perf, ROCm0): TG(32h,d128) 33.96 ->
18.65 us (1.82x); PP-512 610.7 -> 489.6 us (1.25x); PP-1024 1245 ->
996 us. Model-level interleaved A/B vs the 25-patch control (5 rounds,
llama-bench -p 512 -n 128 -r 2): pp512 3926.0 -> 4038.7 (+2.87%),
tg128 117.33 -> 119.99 (+2.26%), arms fully separated.

Gates: test-backend-ops GATED_DELTA_NET all OK (both mappings and the
DPP path exercised); ppl 3.9271/3.9271/3.9278 over 3 loads (-0.11% vs
stock 3.9314, in band). Server greedy smoke at 6 short prompts is
coherent; 3 of 6 drift mid-completion vs control, the expected
reassociation effect of the changed reduction tree (same class as the
0024 multi-row reduction change).
